THOUGHT: This is very interesting! Looking at line 43:
```rust
assert_eq!(pkg.files, ["wasm_pack_bg.wasm"]);
```

So in the test, the expected wasm file is `wasm_pack_bg.wasm`, which is derived from the crate name `wasm-pack` by replacing `-` with `_` and adding `_bg.wasm`.

Looking at the manifest.rs code:
```rust
fn read_cargo_toml(path: &str) -> Result<CargoManifest, Error> {
    let manifest_path = format!("{}/Cargo.toml", path);
    let mut cargo_file = File::open(manifest_path)?;
    let mut cargo_contents = String::new();
    cargo_file.read_to_string(&mut cargo_contents)?;

    Ok(toml::from_str(&cargo_contents)?)
}
```

It reads the Cargo.toml file and parses it. Looking at the CargoPackage struct:
```rust
#[derive(Deserialize)]
struct CargoPackage {
    name: String,
    authors: Vec<String>,
    description: Option<String>,
    version: String,
    license: Option<String>,
    repository: Option<String>,
}
```

So `package.name` gets the name from Cargo.toml. In the case of the wasm-pack project itself, that would be "wasm-pack".

Then in `into_npm`:
```rust
impl CargoManifest {
    fn into_npm(mut self, scope: Option<String>) -> NpmPackage {
        let filename = self.package.name.replace("-", "_");
        let wasm_file = format!("{}_bg.wasm", filename);
        if let Some(s) = scope {
            self.package.name = format!("@{}/{}", s, self.package.name);
        }
        NpmPackage {
            name: self.package.name,
            collaborators: self.package.authors,
            description: self.package.description,
            version: self.package.version,
            license: self.package.license,
            repository: self.package.repository.map(|repo_url| Repository {
                ty: "git".to_string(),
                url: repo_url,
            }),
            files: vec![wasm_file],
            main: "index.js".to_string(),
        }
    }
}
```

So the wasm file gets set to `{filename}_bg.wasm` where filename is the package name with hyphens replaced by underscores. The repository field gets converted to a nested structure with type "git" and the URL from the original manifest.

The main field is hardcoded to "index.js". However, there's a mismatch in bindgen.rs: the code retrieves the original crate name without any transformation, then converts hyphens to underscores for the binary name, but this binary name is used to locate the wasm file at `target/wasm32-unknown-unknown/release/{binary_name}.wasm`. This creates an inconsistency—the manifest expects the wasm file to be named with underscores and a "_bg" suffix, but the build process is looking for it with a different naming convention.

